# L §6.1 (round 14): "same is an equivalence: lines that share a side make one group"; "A group of movements is one
# movement. At a place that two of them touch ... it is booked once"; "a movement listed twice counts once". The
# statement lists one 100.00 PLN payment three times, joined by two same lines that share bank[r32]: konto 1 000.00 -
# 100.00 = 900.00 PLN, and a binding over transfers counts it once. (Was REFCORE-NOT-YET: a movement in two same lines.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source bank_export "wyciąg"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version opening_2026
  cite bank_export
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "saldo"

version statement_01
  cite bank_export
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers konto
  bank[r31] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 31"
  bank[r32] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 32"
  bank[r33] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 33"
  same bank[r32] = bank[r31]
  same bank[r33] = bank[r32]

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
ask n: count(x in transfers over 2026-01)
=== expect
b: 900.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
n: 1
  cut 2026-03-01
